hreat management, sensitive data scanner, and CI visibility. Datadog, Inc. was incorporated in 2010 and is headquartered in New York, New York.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Olivier  Pomel | Co-Founder, CEO & Director | Age 48 | Compensation: $1.2M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 8K people. Revenue per employee of $423K ranks in the above the sector median among Technology peers, with revenue growing 45%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $124K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $93K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 3\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (9/10).","financial_summary":["Datadog, Inc. is a large-cap technology business with a $66.5B market cap on $3.4B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +27% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at -241% against a 11% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests. Gross margins of 79% confirm genuine pricing power.","The business throws off $1.0B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 29 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 9.75\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and thin -4.0\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and stock-based comp at 22% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 658% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":6.577949227051231},{"text":"ROIC sits in the bottom decile among Technology peers \u2014 no moat advantage to speak of","sev":"red","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Operating margins 8% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $95.3M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Technology sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 7% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Elevated sector volatility (38% annualized) adds uncertainty","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Antitrust and platform-regulation risk \u2014 the larger the network effect, the larger the regulatory target on its back, and a single consent decree can reset the moat.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"AI disruption of existing software moats \u2014 incumbents with durable margins face commoditisation as AI-native competitors replicate features at a fraction of the R&D cost.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Cybersecurity liability and talent cost inflation \u2014 a single breach can erase years of goodwill, and the war for engineering talent compresses margins even at scale.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan","Gross margin tops the Technology peer set \u2014 genuine pricing power is present here","Growing faster than most Technology peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool","Among the least levered in Technology \u2014 the fortress balance sheet in its peer set"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Datadog (DDOG) Could Be 32% Undervalued As Strong Earnings Reset The Valuation Debate","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/software/nasdaq-ddog/datadog/news/datadog-ddog-could-be-32-undervalued-as-strong-earnings-rese","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794551937.967,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.904,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"PLTR's Rule of 40 Hits 158%: Can This Momentum Continue?","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3029791/pltr-s-rule-of-40-hits-158-can-this-momentum-continue?cid=CS-ZC-FT-analyst_blog%7Cquick_take-3029791","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794591600.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":2,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"CoreWeave\u2019s Demand is There, $41.6B of Corporate Debt Remains: What This Means for Nebius and CoreWeave","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/technology/ai/articles/coreweave-demand-41-6b-corporate-121513305.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794572113.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.477,"tier":2,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"These 6 Data Software Stocks Help Companies Put AI to Work","source":"aol.com","link":"https://www.aol.com/articles/6-data-software-stocks-help-083302000.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794559097.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.649,"tier":2,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Palantir\u2019s Growth Story Could Be Just Getting Started","source":"aol.com","link":"https://www.aol.com/articles/palantir-growth-story-could-just-163335000.html","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794501800.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.421,"tier":2,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Nebius Tumbles After Trimming 2026 View to Low End of Range","source":"benzinga.com